1
00:00:00,240 --> 00:00:01,920
- Why do you hate me? Just tell me.

2
00:00:01,920 --> 00:00:03,160
- I don’t hate you.

3
00:00:03,280 --> 00:00:05,080
- What do you have to earn my acceptance?

4
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:06,000
- What do you want me to do? 

5
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,600
- Compete against me in a shooting match.

6
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:09,600
- If you win, I’ll accept you.

7
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:10,600
- Don’t be afraid.

8
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:11,560
- Stay focused.

9
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:15,080
- You knew that you could never beat me, 

10
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:16,200
- but you didn’t give up.

11
00:00:16,360 --> 00:00:17,800
- I don’t accept you for your skills, 

12
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:19,200
- but I accept you for your spirit.

13
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:22,520
- Wait for me.

14
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:24,440
- Go away. We are closed.

15
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:25,720
- You can close the application.

16
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:26,960
- I already applied.

17
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:28,560
- Where did you get that confidence?

18
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:33,280
- So? Am I in?

19
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:36,120
- You can’t beat me in everything, Zoe.

20
00:00:37,320 --> 00:00:38,360
- I love you.

21
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:08,920
Hey!

22
00:01:14,440 --> 00:01:15,120
Suea Yai.

23
00:01:23,040 --> 00:01:23,800
Dad.

24
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:14,320
They are not for show. They are for sale.

25
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:17,160
Come and take a look.

26
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,840
The eggplants are fresh.

27
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:23,520
Look. The flies from your shop  
are flying around my vegetables.

28
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:28,000
That’s why no one wants to buy my vegetables.

29
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:30,080
Hey.

30
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:30,560
Hello.

31
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:31,720
The flies are from your shop.

32
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:33,920
I’m here to collect debts.

33
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:34,720
- I’m here to collect debts. 
- Come and take a look.
The vegetables are fresh.

34
00:03:34,720 --> 00:03:38,320
Come and take a look.
The vegetables are fresh.

35
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:39,800
Hello.

36
00:03:40,480 --> 00:03:41,000
- Hello. 
- Come and look at the vegetables.

37
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,880
Come and look at the vegetables.

38
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:45,400
I’m here to collect debts.

39
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:48,880
Don’t take the bad ones.

40
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:51,760
Hongsen sent me to collect debts.

41
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:06,400
Collect debts? 
I haven’t sold anything today.

42
00:04:06,640 --> 00:04:09,160
See and pick what you like.

43
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:14,080
There are plenty. Pick the pretty ones.

44
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:24,800
Here is the money I owe you. 

45
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:25,720
Take it.

46
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:30,640
You know I’m not here  
only to collect the money.

47
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:34,680
Otherwise, you wouldn’t be avoiding me.

48
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:41,160
I heard that you were there that night.

49
00:04:42,920 --> 00:04:44,320
Tell me what you saw.

50
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:47,240
Tell me everything.

51
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:49,000
Every detail.

52
00:04:51,840 --> 00:04:52,840
You saw it, didn’t you?

53
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:55,680
You saw who shot Suea Yai.

54
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:05,240
It’s not working.

55
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:09,720
Den.

56
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:12,120
What?

57
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:14,560
The money.

58
00:05:22,800 --> 00:05:24,200
You collected the debts?

59
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:25,640
I not only collected the debts, 

60
00:05:26,760 --> 00:05:27,840
but I also got snacks from them.

61
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:29,040
Den, have a bite.

62
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:31,680
Thanks.

63
00:05:32,240 --> 00:05:34,320
If you want me to collect debts again, 
just tell me.

64
00:05:35,640 --> 00:05:36,640
I’m now an expert.

65
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:39,360
Stop boasting.

66
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:43,560
Sen.

67
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:44,680
I collected…

68
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:33,960
I want to give you the sweet.

69
00:06:34,880 --> 00:06:36,280
I got it when I went to collect debts.

70
00:06:40,520 --> 00:06:41,240
Keep it.

71
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:44,920
But I saved it for you.

72
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:47,440
Are you sure you don’t want to eat it?

73
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:50,640
It smells good.

74
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:52,360
It’s so sweet.

75
00:06:53,160 --> 00:06:54,040
It’s also delicious.

76
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:56,200
Look at its texture.

77
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:00,640
It looks tasty.

78
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:15,480
So sweet.

79
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:17,960
Go away.

80
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:26,160
I collected the debts.  
Aren’t you going to compliment me?

81
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:30,920
I told you to go away.

82
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:38,600
Are you alright?

83
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:42,760
You have been very quiet 
since you got back from the market.

84
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,240
Why? Did the owner of the photo studio…

85
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:46,360
I want to be alone.

86
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:58,000
If you want to talk, you can tell me.

87
00:07:58,280 --> 00:07:59,000
You can trust me.

88
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:05,040
You can really trust me.

89
00:08:22,640 --> 00:08:23,880
I still can’t find Yong.

90
00:08:24,080 --> 00:08:26,000
I don’t know where your brother is.

91
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:27,120
I’m sure he’s in the hood.

92
00:08:27,280 --> 00:08:28,480
Keep looking for him.

93
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:32,480
Don’t let anyone know 
that Yong is my brother.

94
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:33,840
You know the hood is run by him.

95
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:34,920
Sure.

96
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:37,720
Zoe.

97
00:08:38,880 --> 00:08:39,240
Yes?

98
00:08:39,640 --> 00:08:40,800
Where have you been?

99
00:08:41,040 --> 00:08:43,160
Sorry. I won’t be late again.

100
00:08:43,800 --> 00:08:44,760
I need to get to work.

101
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:47,320
Since he joined our gang, 

102
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:50,240
he sneaks out every morning.

103
00:08:50,640 --> 00:08:51,880
I don’t know where he goes.

104
00:08:52,120 --> 00:08:53,280
When I ask him about his personal life, 

105
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:54,440
he refuses to talk.

106
00:08:54,760 --> 00:08:55,960
He’s so damn secretive.

107
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:58,080
Did you check his background?

108
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:06,240
Thank you, Zeng.

109
00:09:23,920 --> 00:09:24,480
Zeng.

110
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:27,800
Can I take leave the day after tomorrow?

111
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:30,280
I have an errand to do.

112
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:31,480
What errand?

113
00:09:34,400 --> 00:09:35,520
It’s…

114
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:37,960
It’s a personal errand.

115
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:39,120
What personal errand?

116
00:09:39,680 --> 00:09:40,800
I said it’s a personal errand.

117
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:44,360
Isn’t it obvious? It’s personal.

118
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:47,640
It means it’s none of other people’s business.

119
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,000
Are you saying I’m being nosy?

120
00:09:49,760 --> 00:09:51,040
I wasn’t thinking that.

121
00:09:51,760 --> 00:09:53,440
But after hearing you say it, 

122
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:55,400
I started to see it that way.

123
00:09:57,520 --> 00:09:59,240
So I have no right to know your personal life?

124
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:01,240
I’m your gang’s leader.

125
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:03,000
Besides knowing that you are a temple boy, 

126
00:10:03,320 --> 00:10:05,000
I don’t know a damn thing about you.

127
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:10,400
I don’t know anything about you either.

128
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:13,560
And I don’t want to know too.

129
00:10:15,080 --> 00:10:18,640
My gang, we are like a family.

130
00:10:19,040 --> 00:10:20,240
We tell each other everything. 

131
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:22,320
We have each other’s back.

132
00:10:22,920 --> 00:10:24,600
If you can’t do that, 

133
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:27,000
you can’t be a part of my family.

134
00:10:31,800 --> 00:10:32,640
I don’t approve your leave.

135
00:10:36,040 --> 00:10:38,040
I’m docking your pay for being late today.

136
00:11:32,280 --> 00:11:33,040
What are you doing?

137
00:11:39,920 --> 00:11:41,200
Good morning, Father.

138
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:46,520
Why didn’t you tell me?

139
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:48,720
That you’re helping Father 
with the morning alms.

140
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:53,040
Would you believe me if I told you?

141
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:54,880
Why wouldn’t I believe you?

142
00:11:57,320 --> 00:11:58,440
You are prejudiced against me.

143
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:00,200
In your eyes, I’m always wrong.

144
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:01,520
Am I right?

145
00:12:02,400 --> 00:12:03,960
That’s why you secretly followed me.

146
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:06,560
You’re right.

147
00:12:06,800 --> 00:12:07,920
I encountered someone like this before.

148
00:12:08,040 --> 00:12:10,240
If I’m prejudiced against you, 
you should try to earn my trust.

149
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:12,160
Those who regularly pay respect…

150
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:14,200
I’m not acting secretive.

151
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:15,880
But you are prejudiced against me.

152
00:12:16,040 --> 00:12:17,600
So you think I’m acting secretive.

153
00:12:17,600 --> 00:12:18,800
You are acting secretive.

154
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:19,480
You’re prejudiced.

155
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:22,240
When you offer alms, don’t act secretive.

156
00:12:22,240 --> 00:12:22,640
I’m not acting secretive.

157
00:12:22,640 --> 00:12:23,000
You are acting secretive.

158
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:23,360
Hey.

159
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:27,080
You two go act secretive somewhere else.

160
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:28,240
So I can give them a blessing.

161
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:29,680
I’m sorry.

162
00:12:30,800 --> 00:12:33,680
I wish you success and happiness.

163
00:12:38,800 --> 00:12:40,320
Father also agreed that you’re acting secretive.

164
00:12:40,880 --> 00:12:41,480
You will go to hell.

165
00:12:43,560 --> 00:12:44,680
Now, you are in my gang.

166
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:45,720
I need to know about your life.

167
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:47,560
Who are you? 
How did you end up as a temple boy?

168
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:49,000
What have you done? Tell me.

169
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:50,040
Am I being interviewed?

170
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:50,960
Don’t dodge my questions.

171
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:52,200
Tell me. 

172
00:12:52,720 --> 00:12:54,360
Otherwise, I will think that you don’t trust me.

173
00:12:55,360 --> 00:12:56,760
I just have no place to live.

174
00:12:57,760 --> 00:12:59,160
So I asked Father to live at the temple.

175
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:02,080
What about your parents, siblings, or family?

176
00:13:08,880 --> 00:13:09,760
I’m not trying to be nosy.

177
00:13:10,760 --> 00:13:14,400
But if there’s anything I can help you with, 
I want to help.

178
00:13:15,720 --> 00:13:17,600
Everyone in our gang has problems.

179
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:19,960
Don’t tell me that you have no problems.

180
00:13:23,680 --> 00:13:28,040
If you keep your problems to yourself, 
why did you join our gang?

181
00:13:29,360 --> 00:13:30,600
The whole world doesn’t understand us.

182
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:32,800
Only people like us understand each other.

183
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:40,040
I just want you to know.

184
00:13:42,720 --> 00:13:44,240
that you are not alone, Zoe.

185
00:13:53,880 --> 00:13:55,320
It’s not that I don’t trust you.

186
00:13:57,440 --> 00:13:59,080
There’s something I don’t want to talk about.

187
00:14:01,360 --> 00:14:02,960
It’s something I just want to forget.

188
00:14:06,760 --> 00:14:07,120
Alright.

189
00:14:08,280 --> 00:14:09,520
This is good.

190
00:14:09,920 --> 00:14:11,840
At least I know that you have a problem. 

191
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:13,160
You want to forget it, right?

192
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:15,520
Fine, I guarantee you will forget it.

193
00:14:15,920 --> 00:14:19,360
I’ll help you forget everything except me.

194
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:21,320
Let’s go, Zoe.

195
00:14:21,960 --> 00:14:22,440
Let’s roll.

196
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:25,240
Zeng, do I have to remember 
things about you?

197
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:25,720
Watch your step, Zoe.

198
00:14:25,720 --> 00:14:26,600
Let me go.

199
00:14:29,760 --> 00:14:30,480
Damn.

200
00:14:32,400 --> 00:14:33,520
Is this a house or a shack?

201
00:14:38,160 --> 00:14:38,400
Guys.

202
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:45,080
Why don’t you tear it down 
and build a new building?

203
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:47,120
So you can live more comfortably.

204
00:14:47,600 --> 00:14:48,520
Don’t bother.

205
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:51,840
We don’t like owing anyone.

206
00:14:53,760 --> 00:14:55,160
You came all the way here to meet me.

207
00:14:56,160 --> 00:14:57,400
What is your business with me?

208
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:11,840
The election will be held in two months.

209
00:15:12,040 --> 00:15:15,880
I want this side of the river to be developed 
and have good lives like the other side.

210
00:15:19,240 --> 00:15:21,440
I want you to work for me.

211
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:26,120
If you help me, I’ll help you in return.

212
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:29,320
You won’t have to live in this shack 
and have a struggling life. 

213
00:15:29,640 --> 00:15:31,800
You’ll no longer need 
to look over your shoulder for the cops.

214
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:34,840
You already have Zeng working for you.

215
00:15:36,920 --> 00:15:38,640
Zeng has his hands full already.

216
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:41,600
I also don’t want to involve him in this.

217
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:44,760
I want you, Hongsen.

218
00:15:45,560 --> 00:15:47,840
I’m sure you can help me with this.

219
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:50,360
Your name is well-known.

220
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:53,960
Especially what you did to Suea Yai. 

221
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:07,600
We are not capable enough to work for you.

222
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:13,800
You don’t get an opportunity like this every day.

223
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:18,600
You're the first person 
I've come to personally with this opportunity.

224
00:16:35,560 --> 00:16:36,720
Don’t be so hasty.

225
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:39,400
They are country folks.

226
00:16:39,960 --> 00:16:40,920
You should not rush them.

227
00:16:49,920 --> 00:16:50,840
Is he your new member?

228
00:16:58,480 --> 00:16:58,880
Fine.

229
00:17:00,080 --> 00:17:01,360
I’ll give you time to think.

230
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:03,640
Don’t keep me waiting for too long.

231
00:17:06,120 --> 00:17:07,720
People from Phra Nakorn don’t like waiting.

232
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:30,240
I want you, Hongsen.

233
00:17:30,960 --> 00:17:33,000
Your name is well-known.

234
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:36,280
Especially what you did to Suea Yai. 

235
00:17:39,360 --> 00:17:40,560
What did he talk about?

236
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:49,320
Yong.

237
00:17:51,640 --> 00:17:52,080
Yes.

238
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:55,760
You studied accounting, right?

239
00:17:58,680 --> 00:18:00,160
You will take care of our debtor records.

240
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:03,720
You will handle our gang’s accounting.

241
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:07,280
Won’t Den be upset with me? 

242
00:18:07,520 --> 00:18:08,240
He’s managing it.

243
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:09,400
He made mistakes.

244
00:18:10,400 --> 00:18:12,200
That’s why I need to find someone else to do it.

245
00:18:15,640 --> 00:18:15,960
Sure.

246
00:18:20,600 --> 00:18:21,320
Hongsen.

247
00:18:33,600 --> 00:18:38,280
Boss Aang mentioned 
what you did to Suea Yai.

248
00:18:39,520 --> 00:18:40,360
What did you do?

249
00:18:43,600 --> 00:18:45,440
I’m in your gang now.

250
00:18:45,800 --> 00:18:49,440
I just want to boast about it to other people.

251
00:19:08,280 --> 00:19:09,280
hat’s his problem?

252
00:19:16,840 --> 00:19:17,480
Yong.

253
00:19:18,480 --> 00:19:19,680
here’s your head at?

254
00:19:20,840 --> 00:19:21,520
I’m sorry, Den.

255
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:25,480
Den.

256
00:19:27,360 --> 00:19:30,880
Boss Aang mentioned 
that Sen did something to Suea Yai.

257
00:19:31,120 --> 00:19:31,760
What did he do?

258
00:19:32,680 --> 00:19:33,800
Shut up.

259
00:19:34,440 --> 00:19:36,000
This is not something 
you can mention casually.

260
00:19:36,480 --> 00:19:37,240
Why, Den?

261
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:39,840
Is it that serious?

262
00:19:45,080 --> 00:19:45,600
Yong.

263
00:19:49,240 --> 00:19:50,480
Where have you been hiding?

264
00:19:50,880 --> 00:19:53,360
I just remember that 
you have a close friend opening a salon here.

265
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:54,480
Hey.

266
00:19:55,440 --> 00:19:56,200
What are you doing?

267
00:19:59,080 --> 00:19:59,880
Why are you with him?

268
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:01,760
I…

269
00:20:06,880 --> 00:20:07,680
Forget it. Come with me.

270
00:20:14,280 --> 00:20:15,080
You are looking for Mom?

271
00:20:15,920 --> 00:20:17,480
Why are you looking for her?

272
00:20:18,040 --> 00:20:18,960
She left us when we were young.

273
00:20:19,160 --> 00:20:20,760
She didn’t love us. Did you forget that?

274
00:20:21,240 --> 00:20:22,200
No.

275
00:20:23,240 --> 00:20:24,720
f you don’t want to look for her, fine.

276
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:26,320
But I want to look for her.

277
00:20:29,360 --> 00:20:30,480
How did you get involved with Hongsen?

278
00:20:31,920 --> 00:20:32,760
Why are you with his man?

279
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:34,000
He promises he will help me.

280
00:20:34,520 --> 00:20:37,360
Yong, I cut Hongsen off a long time ago.

281
00:20:37,760 --> 00:20:38,840
Why do you ask for his help?

282
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:40,160
How does that have anything to do with me?

283
00:20:41,720 --> 00:20:45,440
Back then, I didn’t want to know 
why you and he stopped being friends.

284
00:20:47,160 --> 00:20:48,360
But now I want to know.

285
00:20:52,560 --> 00:20:53,320
You don’t need to know it.

286
00:20:53,480 --> 00:20:54,120
Come on. Let’s go home.

287
00:20:54,240 --> 00:20:54,840
Wait.

288
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:56,760
Is it about Dad?

289
00:20:58,520 --> 00:20:59,880
That’s why you stopped being his friend.

290
00:21:03,080 --> 00:21:05,200
You told me that Dad was drunk driving 
and ran his car into a tree.

291
00:21:05,360 --> 00:21:06,200
Is it true?

292
00:21:12,280 --> 00:21:13,120
It’s not true, is it?

293
00:21:15,160 --> 00:21:16,480
Have you been lying to me all this time?

294
00:21:16,800 --> 00:21:17,560
Yong.

295
00:21:17,760 --> 00:21:19,440
Don’t I have the right to know how he died?

296
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:22,800
If you lied to me because I was young, 
I can understand that.

297
00:21:23,360 --> 00:21:24,720
But I’m an adult now.

298
00:21:26,120 --> 00:21:27,640
Isn’t it time for me to know the truth?

299
00:21:39,720 --> 00:21:41,200
Hongsen killed Dad.

300
00:21:54,800 --> 00:21:55,360
Sen.

301
00:22:03,760 --> 00:22:05,440
Stop it.

302
00:22:06,720 --> 00:22:07,600
Remember me.

303
00:22:08,400 --> 00:22:09,680
I’m Hongsen.

304
00:22:09,880 --> 00:22:10,480
Asshole!

305
00:22:13,280 --> 00:22:13,680
Come on.

306
00:22:13,680 --> 00:22:14,080
Zeng.

307
00:22:16,120 --> 00:22:19,880
A big shot contacted me about a job.

308
00:22:20,600 --> 00:22:24,240
If I pull it off, he will take good care of me.

309
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:26,160
Who is he?

310
00:22:26,560 --> 00:22:27,280
I don’t know.

311
00:22:28,040 --> 00:22:29,240
The lieutenant is the middleman.

312
00:22:29,800 --> 00:22:31,560
Are you going to work for him 
without knowing who he is?

313
00:22:32,440 --> 00:22:33,200
Are you crazy?

314
00:22:39,880 --> 00:22:40,200
Zeng.

315
00:22:41,720 --> 00:22:44,320
Gangsters like us need powerful people 
in our corner. 

316
00:22:44,800 --> 00:22:45,840
So we can grow more powerful.

317
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:51,240
I won’t let low-ranked cops 
keep picking on us.

318
00:22:57,600 --> 00:23:00,240
Did my dad know about this?

319
00:23:04,880 --> 00:23:05,480
No.

320
00:23:06,800 --> 00:23:07,720
I didn’t tell him.

321
00:23:08,440 --> 00:23:09,720
You can’t tell him either.

322
00:23:11,960 --> 00:23:15,080
I told you because you are my best friend.

323
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:21,880
Come on.

324
00:23:23,720 --> 00:23:24,920
Trust me.

325
00:23:27,360 --> 00:23:28,200
Fine.

326
00:23:29,200 --> 00:23:30,080
You’d better be careful.

327
00:23:31,960 --> 00:23:32,520
I will.

328
00:23:33,160 --> 00:23:34,200
This is more like it.

329
00:23:34,720 --> 00:23:36,280
We always have each other’s backs.

330
00:23:37,120 --> 00:23:38,600
You never listen to my warning anyway.

331
00:23:57,920 --> 00:24:00,400
Come to meet me 
at our meeting point tonight.

332
00:24:01,520 --> 00:24:02,000
As we have agreed.

333
00:24:18,920 --> 00:24:19,440
Zeng.

334
00:24:20,640 --> 00:24:21,120
Dad.

335
00:24:21,840 --> 00:24:22,480
What are you doing?

336
00:24:23,160 --> 00:24:24,280
Are you working with the police?

337
00:24:26,400 --> 00:24:27,400
It’s not your business.

338
00:24:28,400 --> 00:24:29,000
Go home.

339
00:24:29,280 --> 00:24:29,800
Dad.

340
00:24:31,640 --> 00:24:32,200
Go.

341
00:25:33,440 --> 00:25:33,840
Hey.

342
00:25:48,600 --> 00:25:49,280
Dad.

343
00:25:56,720 --> 00:25:58,120
Hongsen, asshole.

344
00:26:04,960 --> 00:26:06,560
F*ck you, Hongsen.

345
00:26:07,520 --> 00:26:09,360
How could you do this to my dad?

346
00:26:09,840 --> 00:26:11,080
Son of a b*tch.

347
00:26:13,840 --> 00:26:14,800
Stop it.

348
00:26:15,680 --> 00:26:17,000
Stop it.

349
00:26:19,320 --> 00:26:20,640
Let me go.

350
00:26:20,640 --> 00:26:21,160
Stop it.

351
00:26:21,400 --> 00:26:23,240
Son of a b*tch. 
Why the hell are you stopping me?

352
00:26:24,880 --> 00:26:25,320
Scumbag.

353
00:26:26,320 --> 00:26:27,560
Why did you kill my dad?

354
00:26:28,040 --> 00:26:28,440
Why?

355
00:26:29,600 --> 00:26:31,840
He was like a father to you.

356
00:26:32,640 --> 00:26:33,840
Scumbag.

357
00:26:34,040 --> 00:26:34,880
Asshole.

358
00:26:38,280 --> 00:26:40,120
I didn’t tell you about this 
because you were young.

359
00:26:41,120 --> 00:26:42,360
You really hated gangsters.

360
00:26:48,240 --> 00:26:49,920
I couldn’t bring myself to tell you the truth.

361
00:26:52,040 --> 00:26:55,600
I promised Dad that I would take care of you 
and wouldn’t hurt you.

362
00:26:58,600 --> 00:26:59,600
You are hurting me.

363
00:27:02,360 --> 00:27:03,360
You lied to me.

364
00:27:06,520 --> 00:27:08,240
You acted like I was not his son.

365
00:27:08,400 --> 00:27:09,040
Yong.

366
00:27:19,760 --> 00:27:20,560
I’m sorry.

367
00:27:23,240 --> 00:27:24,400
Now you know the truth.

368
00:27:26,400 --> 00:27:27,840
Are you still going back to Hongsen?

369
00:27:36,800 --> 00:27:37,920
Leave me alone.

370
00:27:44,680 --> 00:27:45,400
Yong.

371
00:28:29,280 --> 00:28:29,840
Hey.

372
00:28:32,000 --> 00:28:33,080
Don’t be afraid.

373
00:28:41,520 --> 00:28:45,280
Your outfit is not bad, 
but your hair is a mess.

374
00:28:45,640 --> 00:28:47,600
Put oil on your hair. Girls like it.

375
00:29:16,640 --> 00:29:18,200
Den told me that Zeng took you away.

376
00:29:19,280 --> 00:29:20,120
I’m here to take you back.

377
00:29:25,640 --> 00:29:26,840
Is there anything you want to tell me?

378
00:29:33,720 --> 00:29:35,040
Can I trust you?

379
00:29:37,680 --> 00:29:38,720
If I can trust you, 

380
00:29:41,880 --> 00:29:43,080
you can trust me. 

381
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:23,360
Hey.

382
00:30:24,280 --> 00:30:25,040
What’s wrong?

383
00:30:25,720 --> 00:30:26,640
Why the long face?

384
00:30:29,600 --> 00:30:30,560
I want to be alone.

385
00:30:37,080 --> 00:30:38,200
You said you wanted to be alone.

386
00:30:38,720 --> 00:30:40,200
But you came to a crowded place like this.

387
00:30:41,480 --> 00:30:42,720
You don’t mean what you say.

388
00:30:51,880 --> 00:30:53,000
Do you have any siblings?

389
00:30:55,760 --> 00:30:56,400
I’m an only child.

390
00:30:57,480 --> 00:30:57,920
Why?

391
00:31:02,120 --> 00:31:03,280
I have a little brother.

392
00:31:05,320 --> 00:31:08,800
I want to do my best to take care of him 
like I promised my dad.

393
00:31:10,400 --> 00:31:11,440
He doesn’t like gangsters.

394
00:31:11,600 --> 00:31:12,960
I sent him to live with Grandma.

395
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:16,200
So he could grow up to be a good man.

396
00:31:18,120 --> 00:31:19,800
He wouldn’t end up being a gangster like me.

397
00:31:26,640 --> 00:31:27,480
But you know what?

398
00:31:30,320 --> 00:31:33,360
I’m the one who hurt him the most.

399
00:31:37,120 --> 00:31:37,920
Isn’t it ironic?

400
00:31:45,560 --> 00:31:46,800
Did you do that with good intentions?

401
00:31:47,880 --> 00:31:50,720
If your answer is yes,  
then you have nothing to regret.

402
00:31:53,600 --> 00:31:54,640
You did your best.

403
00:31:56,240 --> 00:31:58,240
You should let him choose 
and make decisions for himself.

404
00:31:58,880 --> 00:31:59,840
You can’t force him.

405
00:32:02,720 --> 00:32:03,360
So…

406
00:32:04,440 --> 00:32:05,640
are you telling me to let go?

407
00:32:05,960 --> 00:32:06,480
Yes.

408
00:32:16,880 --> 00:32:17,920
Your shoulders are big.

409
00:32:19,520 --> 00:32:20,520
You must have been carrying a lot of things.

410
00:32:25,800 --> 00:32:26,480
I’ve got to go.

411
00:32:26,880 --> 00:32:28,120
I need to do the shopping for Cheng.

412
00:32:29,280 --> 00:32:31,240
You are a boss. Don’t be a slacker. 

413
00:32:32,400 --> 00:32:33,640
You’re f*cking annoying.

414
00:32:44,400 --> 00:32:45,800
Where did he go?

415
00:33:11,480 --> 00:33:12,280
What are you stressed about?

416
00:33:13,480 --> 00:33:14,800
You look totally defeated.

417
00:33:24,200 --> 00:33:25,400
You are hiding something from me, 
aren’t you?

418
00:33:27,280 --> 00:33:28,760
How could I dare hide anything from you?

419
00:33:31,520 --> 00:33:33,000
There’s no way 
you can hide anything from me.

420
00:33:38,760 --> 00:33:39,600
You knew?

421
00:33:47,760 --> 00:33:49,080
The money that you claimed 
to collect from debtors.

422
00:33:50,160 --> 00:33:51,440
It’s your money, right?

423
00:33:55,960 --> 00:33:57,840
Do you think I’ve never done it?

424
00:33:58,960 --> 00:33:59,720
I’ve done it all.

425
00:34:05,320 --> 00:34:06,200
When you were with Suea Yai?

426
00:34:13,320 --> 00:34:14,200
Why are you asking about him?

427
00:34:15,720 --> 00:34:16,280
Nothing.

428
00:34:17,440 --> 00:34:18,680
I’m just curious.

429
00:34:19,280 --> 00:34:21,480
I heard Boss Aang talked about 
your history with Suea Yai.

430
00:34:23,120 --> 00:34:24,880
Why have you never told me about it?

431
00:34:25,320 --> 00:34:26,800
You have heard about it, haven’t you?

432
00:34:30,440 --> 00:34:31,280
Did you really kill him?

433
00:34:47,680 --> 00:34:48,800
I was framed.

434
00:34:49,920 --> 00:34:50,880
I took the job 

435
00:34:51,440 --> 00:34:52,800
because I wanted to have powerful people 
backing me.

436
00:34:53,200 --> 00:34:55,520
I didn’t want to be a stooge for the cops 
for the rest of my life.

437
00:34:56,080 --> 00:34:57,840
If I knew the target was Suea Yai, 

438
00:34:58,240 --> 00:34:59,360
I would have never taken the job.

439
00:34:59,880 --> 00:35:01,560
I would never betray him.

440
00:35:02,360 --> 00:35:03,880
Did you take the job to kill me?

441
00:35:05,480 --> 00:35:05,840
No.

442
00:35:06,400 --> 00:35:07,320
Don’t lower your gun.

443
00:35:09,040 --> 00:35:10,080
They are watching you.

444
00:35:14,720 --> 00:35:18,160
They told me that this would be my last job.

445
00:35:20,480 --> 00:35:21,400
Now they are done with me, 

446
00:35:22,560 --> 00:35:24,160
they want to get rid of me like I was a dog.

447
00:35:25,720 --> 00:35:27,080
They hired you to kill me 

448
00:35:28,240 --> 00:35:30,200
because I know too much about them.

449
00:35:32,800 --> 00:35:34,080
I didn’t know that the target was you.

450
00:35:34,600 --> 00:35:36,200
Hongsen, listen to me.

451
00:35:38,160 --> 00:35:39,640
They will kill us both.

452
00:35:41,400 --> 00:35:46,360
Our lives will never get better 
as long as they are still here.

453
00:35:50,720 --> 00:35:51,440
Dad.

454
00:36:03,640 --> 00:36:06,400
He was shot by a sniper.

455
00:36:14,960 --> 00:36:15,560
What’s wrong?

456
00:36:22,560 --> 00:36:23,440
I…

457
00:36:25,600 --> 00:36:26,800
I think we should go back.

458
00:36:42,960 --> 00:36:43,720
Boss.

459
00:36:45,120 --> 00:36:46,000
Why are you still up?

460
00:36:47,800 --> 00:36:50,680
Don’t tell me 
that you stayed up waiting for me?

461
00:36:53,040 --> 00:36:54,400
You left it at Cheng’s shop.

462
00:36:55,440 --> 00:36:56,800
I followed you to return it.

463
00:36:57,640 --> 00:36:59,040
But I saw that you were busy. 

464
00:36:59,280 --> 00:37:00,520
So I didn’t give it back.

465
00:37:44,920 --> 00:37:45,480
Zeng.

466
00:37:49,080 --> 00:37:50,640
You saw me with a cop, right?

467
00:37:57,520 --> 00:38:00,320
Do you know how a snitch usually ends up?

468
00:38:03,000 --> 00:38:04,360
They either end up dead or in prison. 

469
00:38:05,440 --> 00:38:08,000
Even if you go to jail, 
you will be killed later anyway.

470
00:38:08,440 --> 00:38:09,360
I’m not working for them.

471
00:38:09,360 --> 00:38:10,480
Don’t lie to me.

472
00:38:11,440 --> 00:38:12,600
I’m telling you this.

473
00:38:13,400 --> 00:38:15,400
No matter what they promise you, 

474
00:38:16,440 --> 00:38:18,320
when you are no longer useful to them, 

475
00:38:21,200 --> 00:38:22,160
they won’t keep you around.

476
00:38:30,240 --> 00:38:31,440
You saw me with the police.

477
00:38:34,480 --> 00:38:35,240
It’s because of this.

478
00:38:47,480 --> 00:38:48,480
I got it when I was in there.

479
00:38:53,080 --> 00:38:54,280
I was in prison.

480
00:38:56,440 --> 00:38:58,400
They beat me so badly that I almost died.

481
00:38:58,760 --> 00:38:59,920
I needed to make some allies.

482
00:39:01,080 --> 00:39:02,560
Otherwise, I wouldn’t have been alive today.

483
00:39:05,360 --> 00:39:06,160
What about that cop?

484
00:39:10,800 --> 00:39:14,440
He was the one who arrested me.

485
00:39:15,160 --> 00:39:16,200
When I was released from prison, 

486
00:39:16,640 --> 00:39:17,800
he started extorting money from me.

487
00:39:19,720 --> 00:39:21,120
If I don’t pay him every month, 

488
00:39:22,200 --> 00:39:25,480
he will find a way 
to throw me back into prison.

489
00:39:30,000 --> 00:39:31,680
If you don’t trust me, I get it.

490
00:39:34,520 --> 00:39:35,840
I’m just an ex-con.

491
00:39:39,480 --> 00:39:40,640
You wouldn’t trust me.

492
00:39:43,120 --> 00:39:44,760
Why didn’t you tell me about it?

493
00:39:50,960 --> 00:39:52,480
It’s something I want to forget.

494
00:39:55,040 --> 00:39:56,120
You would never understand me.

495
00:39:57,880 --> 00:39:59,000
If I don’t understand you, 

496
00:40:00,840 --> 00:40:02,400
no one in this world would.

497
00:40:06,800 --> 00:40:07,920
I accept you into my gang.

498
00:40:08,720 --> 00:40:10,400
It means you are now a part of my family.

499
00:40:11,360 --> 00:40:15,040
Family members don’t have secrets 
from each other.

500
00:40:16,800 --> 00:40:18,800
I don’t care if you are an ex-con.

501
00:40:19,560 --> 00:40:23,120
My point is that I trust you.

502
00:40:24,880 --> 00:40:25,440
What about you?

503
00:40:26,880 --> 00:40:28,000
Can I trust you?

504
00:40:35,480 --> 00:40:36,840
Look at me in the eyes 

505
00:40:38,320 --> 00:40:39,240
and tell me.

506
00:40:40,720 --> 00:40:42,200
Can I trust you?

507
00:40:46,720 --> 00:40:49,720
You can trust me.

508
00:40:56,240 --> 00:40:56,760
Good.

509
00:40:58,760 --> 00:40:59,600
That’s all.

510
00:41:01,640 --> 00:41:02,160
Come on.

511
00:41:12,680 --> 00:41:13,200
Let’s go.

512
00:41:13,520 --> 00:41:14,240
Let’s take a shower.

513
00:41:14,840 --> 00:41:15,360
Take a shower?

514
00:41:15,440 --> 00:41:15,720
Yes.

515
00:41:16,480 --> 00:41:17,360
We are half naked. 

516
00:41:17,360 --> 00:41:18,280
We need to take a shower.

517
00:41:18,920 --> 00:41:19,240
Come on.

518
00:41:20,920 --> 00:41:21,920
Right.

519
00:41:27,720 --> 00:41:28,360
Zoe.

520
00:41:28,920 --> 00:41:29,680
What were you arrested for?

521
00:41:31,200 --> 00:41:31,640
Drugs.

522
00:41:32,520 --> 00:41:33,720
I was set up.

523
00:41:33,880 --> 00:41:35,480
Why can't my lottery predictions 
be this accurate?

524
00:41:35,840 --> 00:41:38,040
They always use this dirty trick. 
They are scumbags.

525
00:41:38,840 --> 00:41:39,720
I’m so pissed.

526
00:41:41,680 --> 00:41:42,600
Are you going to take a shower alone?

527
00:41:42,600 --> 00:41:43,760
Go get the water bowl behind you.

528
00:41:56,960 --> 00:41:57,760
Give me the soap.

529
00:41:58,120 --> 00:41:59,480
You’ve been wetting your body for a while.

530
00:41:59,480 --> 00:42:01,360
Are you taking a shower 
without applying soap?

531
00:42:01,360 --> 00:42:02,080
You are nagging so much.

532
00:42:02,080 --> 00:42:03,320
Here. Take it.

533
00:42:21,040 --> 00:42:22,200
He’s smiling cutely, right?

534
00:42:24,640 --> 00:42:25,640
He looks happy.

535
00:42:26,160 --> 00:42:26,840
I envy him.

536
00:42:27,520 --> 00:42:30,040
He was forced to take the picture.

537
00:42:30,320 --> 00:42:33,520
Before he smiled like this, 
his mom hit him several times.

538
00:42:34,280 --> 00:42:38,800
After I took his picture, he kicked my glass cabinet, broke it, and ran away.

539
00:42:41,880 --> 00:42:44,120
Pictures only capture a moment in their life.

540
00:42:45,000 --> 00:42:46,200
If you judged him from the picture, 

541
00:42:47,040 --> 00:42:48,480
you would think that he was happy.

542
00:42:49,480 --> 00:42:50,680
But if you look carefully, 

543
00:42:51,560 --> 00:42:52,800
you will see the story behind it.

544
00:42:53,440 --> 00:42:54,720
It could be something completely different.

545
00:42:55,560 --> 00:42:59,600
You can’t judge someone 
based on what other people see.

546
00:43:01,600 --> 00:43:03,240
What should I do?

547
00:43:03,600 --> 00:43:05,000
You need to trust your own judgement.

548
00:43:12,080 --> 00:43:13,000
Thank you.

549
00:43:14,120 --> 00:43:14,720
I’ve got to go.

550
